From 4ce94a637a5a39e189f4f77a65927867b4a444c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CreateCVOnline <dev@createcvonline.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 15:43:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Make all three template galleries statically rendered
 (audit 3.4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

/templates was the most linked page on the site and the only marketing page
rendered per request: every filter was a next/link writing to the query
string, and reading searchParams — in the body or in generateMetadata — opts
a route into dynamic rendering.

The query string was doing two unrelated jobs, so the fix splits them.
Category becomes a row of links to the six static category pages, which
already had their own copy and were being competed with by ?category=; plan,
columns, ATS and search become client-side filtering over cards the server
has already rendered, matched through data- attributes so the registry never
reaches the browser. With JavaScript off the page is the full gallery.

The ?category= redirect lives in proxy.ts rather than next.config.ts: a
redirects() rule forwards the query it matched on and would land on
/templates/modern?category=modern, inventing a third address.

Writing the regression test against all three galleries rather than just the
English one is what surfaced the rest of this change. It failed on
TemplateFilterBar being absent from the French and German pages — the English
gallery had gained search and filters the localised ones did not have — and
verifying the fix in a browser turned up four more defects:

- The French and German ItemList pointed at English URLs and English preview
  images, contradicting the hreflang cluster the pages sit inside.
- The search box could not match French or German at all. The haystack is the
  registry's metadata and the registry has one language, so banque, étudiant
  and minimaliste returned nothing — the three examples the French
  placeholder itself suggested. lib/i18n/search-terms.ts translates the query
  rather than the corpus.
- Splitting a phrase into words is wrong: "two column" as two AND column
  matched a one-column template whose tagline reads "a two-line name". The
  registry has 17 two-column templates; the three languages had been
  returning 20, 17 and 32 for the same question.
- SiteFooter asked locale === 'fr' before using a translation, so every
  German page shipped an English footer, blurb included. The German copy had
  been correct in nav.ts the whole time, which is what made it invisible.

Both new test files assert on the rendered component rather than the copy
table, because that is the second time a translation has been present and
unused.

Verified: 1,595 tests; ○ for all three galleries; SEO check 268 pages, 0
errors, 0 warnings; browser pass over all three locales.

